    "body": "### Problem\n\nAndroid 14, Termux; nvim 0.12, 0.13\nIssue appeared after the update. Horizontal splitting and then scrolling in any way the active window affects the rows of the other window. It seems like inactive window is being \"scrolled\", while actually cursor there doesn't change it's actual position (which is noticeable after Ctrl+L). Interface is also being broken (scrolled) by the bug.\n\nIssue can be partially fixed by :set laststatus=0. In that way, both windows scrolling works properly.\nUntil we split one of the windows horizontally. Now scrolling the new window scrolls other content on the horizontal line again, despite laststatus=0.\n\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d186a385-6e5d-4161-8145-431ff4e27cef\n\nVim has no same issues.\nPC build works correctly.\nThe problem is, now stable version from pkg causes this bug.\n\nVersions:\n0.11.6 (built from source now; installed before update from pkg) - works correctly ✅\n0.12.3-1 (from pkg install neovim) - bug appears ❌\n0.13.0-dev (from pkg install neovim-nightly) - bug appears ❌\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- open clean neovim\nnvim --clean\n:edit *any big file*\n:vsplit\n- try to scroll (gestures, scroll, arrows)\n**Another (inactive) window being affected by scrolling; lines of text eventually being replaced by blank lines.**\n- update screen <Ctrl+L>\n**All windows fixed untill the other scroll.**\n- remove bar :set laststatus=0\n- try to scroll again, switch between windows, etc\n**Scrolling works correctly for now.**\n- split one of the windows horizontally.\n**Now new small window has bar underneath despite laststatus=0**\n- try to scroll other windows\n**Expected behaviour.**\n- try to scroll small window\n**Stated issue reappears. It affects ONLY lines taken horizontally by a small window.**\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nBehaviour of previous versions of nvim, like 0.11.6.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.13.0-dev (pkg nightly), 0.12.3 (pkg)\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno, vim version 9.2.700\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nAndroid 14\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nTERMUX_VERSION=googleplay.2026.06.21\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\npkg install neovim (0.12.3), pkg install neovim-nightly (0.13.0), build from source",
